From: Julius Bairaktaris <julius@bairaktaris.de>
Subject: [PATCH] ath11k: authorise open-network peers in the NSS firmware

The NSS firmware drops the frames of a peer it has not been told is
authorised, and it is told when a key is installed or, for a mesh peer,
when the station is authorised. A peer on an open access point or
station vdev installs no key. Authorise every peer in the firmware when
mac80211 authorises the station.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Julius Bairaktaris <julius@bairaktaris.de>
---
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/mac.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/mac.c
@@ -10315,11 +10315,10 @@ static int ath11k_mac_op_sta_state(struc
 
 		spin_unlock_bh(&ar->ab->base_lock);
 
-		/* An open mesh installs no key, which is where the firmware
-		 * is otherwise told a peer may pass frames.
+		/* An open network installs no key, which is where the
+		 * firmware is otherwise told a peer may pass frames.
 		 */
-		if (ar->ab->nss_offload && peer_id &&
-		    vif->type == NL80211_IFTYPE_MESH_POINT)
+		if (ar->ab->nss_offload && peer_id)
 			nss_wifi_peer_authorize(ar->ab->nss_soc, peer_id);
 
 		if (vif->type == NL80211_IFTYPE_STATION && arvif->is_up) {
